\f0\fs22
Live Chat Demo - README\par
\par
overview\par
- Self-hosted live chat demo with real-time 1:1 and group chat, retractable right-side contacts, bottom chat windows, typing/beep, file/photo/video sharing, click-to-start video, presence colors (green online, gray offline), contact search, add contact, and a single silent auto-add trigger.\par
- Emoji support: emojis work when typed; optional emoji picker button can be enabled.\par
\par
features included\par
- Real-time 1:1 and group chat\par
- Retractable right-side contacts/groups with avatars\par
- Bottom-docked chat windows (minimize/restore)\par
- Typing indicator with beep on receive\par
- File/photo/video attachments\par
- Click-to-start video calls\par
- Presence colors: green = online, gray = offline (optional away)\par
- Search contacts field\par
- Add contact field (by username/email, saved)\par
- Silent auto-add at one workflow point (no pop-up)\par
\par
requirements\par
- Node.js 18+ and a reverse proxy (Apache or Nginx) with SSL\par
- SQLite by default; MySQL or MariaDB optional\par
\par
quick install\par
1) Upload the provided package to your server, for example: /var/www/chat\par
2) In that folder, install dependencies:\par
   npm ci\par
3) Copy the environment file:\par
   cp .env.example .env\par
4) Set these in .env:\par
   APP_URL=https://chat.yourdomain.com\par
   PORT=3000\par
   SESSION_SECRET=replace_me\par
   DB_DIALECT=sqlite\par
   SQLITE_FILE=./data/chat.sqlite\par
   MYSQL_HOST=...\par
   MYSQL_USER=...\par
   MYSQL_PASSWORD=...\par
   MYSQL_DATABASE=...\par
   EMOJI_PICKER=0 or 1\par
   IDLE_MINUTES=5\par
5) Initialize storage (creates tables if missing):\par
   npm run db:init\par
6) Start the service (or use pm2/systemd):\par
   npm start\par
\par
reverse proxy example (nginx)\par
- Proxy your chat subdomain to http://127.0.0.1:3000 and enable WebSocket upgrade:\par
\par
   server {\par
     listen 443 ssl;\par
     server_name chat.yourdomain.com;\par
\par
     location / {\par
       proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:3000;\par
       proxy_http_version 1.1;\par
       proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;\par
       proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";\par
       proxy_set_header Host $host;\par
     }\par
   }\par
\par
apache note\par
- For Apache, enable ProxyPass and ProxyPassReverse and be sure to allow WebSocket upgrade (Upgrade and Connection headers).\par
\par
sso integration (simple)\par
- The chat trusts these headers from your app’s server-side only when proxying:\par
  X-User-Id, X-User-Name, X-User-Email, X-User-Avatar\par
- Set them for authenticated users when proxying to the chat.\par
- For quick testing, passing ?u=DisplayName on the demo URL also works.\par
\par
silent auto-add hook (one workflow point)\par
- Call this server-to-server when your workflow event fires:\par
  POST /api/contacts/auto-add\par
  body: { "owner_id": "<your_user_id>", "contact_id": "<other_user_id>" }\par
- Returns 200 if the contact is added; no pop-up shown.\par
\par
presence colors\par
- Green = online, gray = offline. Optional away if user idle exceeds IDLE_MINUTES.\par
\par
search and add contact\par
- Search filters by name/email in the contacts list.\par
- Add contact supports by username/email and stores it in the contacts table.\par
\par
emoji option\par
- If EMOJI_PICKER=1, an emoji picker button is shown; otherwise users can type emojis normally.\par
\par
deployment guidance\par
- Install on staging first.\par
- Use a separate subdomain or folder.\par
- Use separate tables or a distinct table prefix.\par
- Avoid altering existing PHP/CodeIgniter routes and code.\par
- Keep assets under their own path to prevent collisions.\par
\par
troubleshooting\par
- If WebSockets do not connect, verify reverse proxy Upgrade and Connection headers.\par
- If presence does not change, check server time and IDLE_MINUTES.\par
- For MySQL, ensure charset=utf8mb4 and collation=utf8mb4_unicode_ci.\par
\par
handover\par
- Package includes source code, .env example, and this README.\par
- Ownership: self-hosted, no subscriptions.\par
}
